27).\n- **Debt:** The market is open but costlier. Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably (utility-credit). Pellham appears unable to close its gap with debt alone. I found no data on its credit metrics, so I can't say whether it is constrained or has chosen not to borrow more.\n- **Equity:** The market is weak. Pellham withdrew its C$2.4B offering because demand fell short. Two other utility offerings were cut back in Q3 2026 (pellham-offering, utility-credit).\n- **Consequence:** Pellham is cutting 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and deferring two substation programmes until financing improves. As the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria, its cuts will probably hurt equipment suppliers.\n\nPlans that lean on equity are at risk. Plans that can be funded with debt, like Norvane's, look fundable.\n\n**Gaps:** I found no figures for total 2027 funding needs, debt capacity, rating headroom, bond maturities, or Norvane's equity plans. I also don't know whether the equity market will reopen.\n\nDetails are in n5.r1 (debt) and n6.r1 (equity).","ttft_ms":2305,"type":"result","duration_ms":33192,"uuid":"6cba6aab-856d-4555-9ba0-cb991d22301a","ttft_stream_ms":2104,"time_to_request_ms":843,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":45,"system_prompt":23,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":33,"input_attachments":67,"input_hooks":8,"conversation_append":14,"transcript_persist":83,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":94,"init_frame_send":21,"engine_pickup":11,"loop_entry":25,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":9,"autocompact":34,"request_announcements":177,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":9,"tool_schema_build":35,"message_normalization":41,"client_creation":57,"request_build":54},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":642,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":176,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":183,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":109,"process_rss_mib_result